IMPORT prelude

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore) -- PART 9, MATERNITY PROTECTION AND BENEFITS
-- AND CHILDCARE LEAVE FOR PARENT, ss 76 to 83.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/EmA1968.txt
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No
-- pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- THE CURRENT LAW ONLY. s 76 carries three qualifying rules side by side --
-- s 76(2) for children delivered before 1 May 2013, s 76(2A) for 1 May 2013 to
-- 22 August 2015, and s 76(2B) for 22 August 2015 onwards -- and ss 84 and 84A
-- do the same for dismissal. Only the CURRENT limb, s 76(2B), is encoded. A
-- confinement before 22 August 2015 is outside this encoding entirely, and the
-- rules for it are different. That is a deliberate scope choice and it is the
-- first thing to check before relying on anything here.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: ss 84, 84A (dismissal without sufficient cause or on grounds of
-- redundancy before confinement, each with its own historical limbs), s 85,
-- s 87 (contracting out), s 87A (childcare leave), and the Fifth Schedule
-- reckoning used by s 76(1)(c)(ii).

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 9`

§§ `76(1) -- the three ways of taking the absence`

-- s 76(1): every female employee is entitled to absent herself from work --
--   (a) 4 weeks immediately BEFORE confinement and 8 weeks immediately AFTER;
--   (b) a single period of 12 weeks, as agreed, starting no earlier than 28 days
--       before and no later than the day of confinement; or
--   (c) 8 weeks as agreed on the same start window, PLUS further periods agreed
--       between them, in aggregate no shorter than the Fifth Schedule reckoning
--       or 24 days whichever is lower, all within 12 months of confinement.
--
-- Sixteen weeks in total under (a) and (b). (c) is the flexible arrangement:
-- 8 weeks around the birth and the balance taken in pieces across the year.
DECLARE AbsenceArrangement IS ONE OF
    `the default -- 4 weeks before and 8 weeks after`           -- s 76(1)(a)
    `a single agreed period of 12 weeks`                        -- s 76(1)(b)
    `8 agreed weeks plus further agreed periods within 12 months` -- s 76(1)(c)

-- s 76(1A): the BENEFIT PERIOD -- the part of the absence that is PAID -- is
-- shorter than the absence in two of the three cases:
--   (a) the 4 weeks before plus THE FIRST 4 WEEKS of the 8 weeks after = 8 weeks;
--   (b) THE FIRST 8 WEEKS of the 12 = 8 weeks;
--   (c) the 8 weeks referred to in (1)(c)(i) = 8 weeks.
--
-- So the benefit period is 8 weeks on every arrangement, and under (a) and (b)
-- the employee may be absent for longer than she is paid for.
GIVEN `the arrangement` IS AN AbsenceArrangement
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the weeks of absence under section 76(1)` IS
    CONSIDER `the arrangement`
    WHEN `the default -- 4 weeks before and 8 weeks after` THEN 12
    WHEN `a single agreed period of 12 weeks` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 8

GIVEN `the arrangement` IS AN AbsenceArrangement
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the weeks of the benefit period under section 76(1A)` IS
    CONSIDER `the arrangement`
    WHEN `the default -- 4 weeks before and 8 weeks after` THEN 8
    WHEN `a single agreed period of 12 weeks` THEN 8
    OTHERWISE 8

GIVEN `the arrangement` IS AN AbsenceArrangement
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the weeks of absence that are unpaid` IS
    `the weeks of absence under section 76(1)` `the arrangement`
        MINUS `the weeks of the benefit period under section 76(1A)` `the arrangement`

§§ `76(2B) -- the qualifying service for payment`

-- s 76(2B): a female employee who delivers on or after 22 August 2015 (or
-- before, with an estimated delivery date on or after) "is NOT entitled to any
-- pay during the benefit period if she has NOT SERVED her employer for a period
-- of AT LEAST 3 MONTHS preceding the day of her confinement."
--
-- Expressed negatively, like ss 45 and 46: it bars payment below the threshold
-- rather than conferring it above.
DECLARE MaternityFacts HAS
    `the arrangement`                           IS AN AbsenceArrangement
    `delivered on or after 22 August 2015, or with an estimated delivery date on or after that day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months served preceding the day of confinement` IS A NUMBER
    `the gross rate of pay for one day`         IS A NUMBER
    -- s 76(3): a day worked during the benefit period before confinement.
    `days worked during the benefit period before confinement` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 83
    `has worked for another employer after absenting herself under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A MaternityFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 76(2B) governs the entitlement` IF
    `the facts`'s `delivered on or after 22 August 2015, or with an estimated delivery date on or after that day`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A MaternityFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `payment during the benefit period is barred for want of service` IF
        `section 76(2B) governs the entitlement` `the facts`
    AND `the facts`'s `months served preceding the day of confinement` LESS THAN 3

-- s 83: "If a female employee works for ANY OTHER EMPLOYER after she has
-- absented herself from work under the provisions of this Part, she FORFEITS
-- her claim to any payment ... AND IS LIABLE TO DISMISSAL."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A MaternityFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim to payment is forfeited under section 83` IF
    `the facts`'s `has worked for another employer after absenting herself under this Part`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A MaternityFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `she is entitled to payment during the benefit period` IF
        `section 76(2B) governs the entitlement` `the facts`
    AND NOT `payment during the benefit period is barred for want of service` `the facts`
    AND NOT `the claim to payment is forfeited under section 83` `the facts`

-- The amount, at the gross rate of pay for the benefit period. 7 days a week,
-- because the benefit period is stated in weeks of absence rather than in
-- working days.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A MaternityFacts
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the payment for the benefit period` IS
    IF   NOT `she is entitled to payment during the benefit period` `the facts`
    THEN 0
    ELSE (`the weeks of the benefit period under section 76(1A)` (`the facts`'s `the arrangement`)
              TIMES 7)
             TIMES `the facts`'s `the gross rate of pay for one day`

-- s 76(3): where she has WORKED on a day during the benefit period before
-- confinement, she is entitled, IN ADDITION to her gross rate of pay for that
-- day, to either another day's pay or a day's absence at the end of the benefit
-- period. So a day worked in the benefit period is paid twice over.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A MaternityFacts
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the additional payment for days worked in the benefit period` IS
    `the facts`'s `days worked during the benefit period before confinement`
        TIMES `the facts`'s `the gross rate of pay for one day`

§§ `81 and 82 -- protection during the absence`

-- s 81: "when a female employee absents herself from work in accordance with
-- the provisions of this Part it is NOT LAWFUL for her employer to give her
-- notice of dismissal DURING her absence OR ON SUCH A DAY THAT THE NOTICE WILL
-- EXPIRE DURING HER ABSENCE."
--
-- Two limbs, and the second is the one that does the work: an employer cannot
-- time a notice so that it lands inside the protected period.
GIVEN `the employee is absent in accordance with this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `notice of dismissal was given during the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the notice would expire during the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice of dismissal is unlawful under section 81` IF
        `the employee is absent in accordance with this Part`
    AND `the notice falls within either limb of section 81` `notice of dismissal was given during the absence` `the notice would expire during the absence`

GIVEN `notice of dismissal was given during the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the notice would expire during the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice falls within either limb of section 81` IF
        `notice of dismissal was given during the absence`
    OR  `the notice would expire during the absence`

-- s 82: "Any employer who KNOWINGLY employs a female employee at any time
-- during the period of 4 WEEKS immediately following her confinement shall be
-- guilty of an offence."
--
-- Note the direction. This is not a protection the employee may waive by
-- agreeing to come back: it is an offence by the employer, and the only mental
-- element is knowledge of the employment, not of any objection.
GIVEN `the employer employed her during the 4 weeks immediately following confinement` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the employer knew` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is guilty of an offence under section 82` IF
        `the employer employed her during the 4 weeks immediately following confinement`
    AND `the employer knew`
